WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:12.800
Today I'm going to show you 4 cool tricks

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.260
That you can practice at home!

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.280
This first one hasn't really got
anything to do with table tennis

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:23.820
But it's a cool party trick

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.160
And all you need
is one table tennis ball

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.960
The idea is to create a trap of air

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.040
Between your hands

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:33.480
So when you hit it

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.700
The ball will pop out

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.440
And it makes a cool sound

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.740
This one is actually not that difficult

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.840
if you know the technique

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:44.800
So the first step is to wrap your fingers around the ball

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.640
So no air can slip through

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.240
Once you have found the grip

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.480
You create a cup

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.940
with the rest of your fingers

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:54.360
The most important thing is not to squeeze the ball hard

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:57.500
It just has to be really gently on top
- just so it covers everything

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.360
Otherwise it won't come off when you hit

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.260
But if it's gently there

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:05.160
It comes off

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.840
Another thing is you don't hit it with your hand

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:12.040
The hand isn't hitting the ball in the air
- it's the pressure that pops it out

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.080
So all you need is a gentle tap
if you have the right grip

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:25.900
So this next one is actually quite good
practice for ball control

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:31.400
The idea is to roll the ball onto the
other side of the racket without the ball bouncing

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:36.820
And of course if you're a
beginner there's a lot of easier variations

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:38.300
If you want to start off with
these

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.440
Basically anything you do with the racket and the ball

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:48.700
Is good practice for control

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:52.280
So you can come up with whatever variations you want

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:02.560
Okay so this one won't make you
a better table tennis player

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:03.060
But

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.620
It makes you into a
cooler table tennis player

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:09.020
So all it is

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:12.660
is just one spin on your finger

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:15.600
And to do this

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.460
You give speed with your wrist

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:18.840
And just spin it over

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:20.640
And catch with your thumb

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:23.320
It's also important to spin it counterclockwise

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:25.700
because if you spin it clockwise

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:27.420
It's a lot harder to catch

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:30.420
Yeah, no. Doesn't work.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:32.240
So you spin it this way

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.580
And if you want to take it further you can do the double spin

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:36.740
Triple spin

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.720
It's maybe best to practice this on top of something soft

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:44.350
Maybe this isn't so useless after all

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:45.560
You could come up with a...

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:49.820
cool serve to
fool your opponent or something

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:51.500
Or maybe not.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:07.180
This one is quite hard to do

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.040
But if you can generate spin

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.520
It's not that hard to catch it with your nails

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.780
If you want to practice putting
spin on the ball

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.600
You can do it for example on the table

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:18.620
Just get below the ball

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:20.860
And hit it to the side

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:24.760
This is also really good practice for
controlling the ball

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.860
And understanding how spin works

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:31.320
So with your nails you form
a sort of circle

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:33.300
You don't even need to use all five fingers

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:36.020
I use four because it just feels more natural

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:38.920
After that all you need to do

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.560
is to catch it on your nails

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.780
If you want to put even more spin on the ball

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:45.880
You can throw the ball at the racket

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:47.640
And then catch it

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:54.720
This is also a pretty
useful way to check if the ball is round

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.560
Because if the ball is round

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:59.300
It's not gonna wobble

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:00.900
It's gonna have a smooth spin

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:02.920
And also you can hear it from
the sound

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:05.800
So for example this ball is really bad

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:08.300
It wobbles

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:10.700
And this one is good

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:12.260
It's a clean spin

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.640
So hope you guys learnt something

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.280
And got some fun ideas
to practice

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.080
Until next time!

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:30.820
Triple spin

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:33.140
So close!

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.100
1, 2, 3!

